  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Status: designed, not yet run on the Pi",
      "items": [
        "The ontology says what runs where: the bridge, Omi Assist and the Thymio link on the Pi; the face, vision, reading and speech on the phone; the setup page on a PC (omi_robot.ttl 111–122). The same image and launch file as in the lab (start.sh 118–120); the Pi needs Docker, its arm64 build of the image, and adb.",
        "Both cables are the Pi's USB: the phone (data through adb reverse, and charging) and the Thymio (omi_robot.ttl 96–106). The Pi needs 5 V and 3 A; a power bank on the robot changes its balance (omi_robot.ttl 151–155)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Reaching it from a PC",
      "items": [
        "/api and a keyless /ws/mirror answer loopback only (wsserver.py 322–330, 343–352). A PC or tablet on the Wi-Fi opens an SSH tunnel to the Pi and then uses http://localhost:8782/setup.html: to the bridge it is loopback, so the setup page, the Webots mirror and a shown picture (Zeigen) work as in the lab (README.md 58–61).",
        "The phone stays on USB, so its page is still localhost: no certificate is needed on the robot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What changes from the lab",
      "items": [
        "Only where things run: the topics, the pages and the programs are the same, so a program tested in the lab runs unchanged on the robot (contract.py 22–25).",
        "Webots stays on the PC: the twin mirrors the robot through the tunnel and rejoins when the Pi's bridge restarts (atl_phone_twin.py 818–832)."
      ]
    }
  ]
